---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Placeholder domain, unconfirmed — change here once and it flows everywhere below.
const SITE = 'https://crossagent.dev';
---

<Base
  title="crossagent — your agent needs a second opinion"
  description="crossagent pairs the coding agent in one tmux pane with the one next to it. One writes, the other pushes back, before you ever see the diff."
>

<header class="band band--hero" id="pair">
  <div class="inner hero">
    <div class="hero__copy">
      <h1><span class="nb">Your agent</span><br><span class="nb">needs a <em class="reviews">second</em></span><br><em class="reviews">opinion.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero__sub"><strong>crossagent</strong> pairs the coding agent in one tmux pane with the one next to it. One writes, the other pushes back, before you ever see the diff.</p>

      <dl class="hero__for">
        <dt>FOR</dt>
        <dd>developers who already run more than one coding agent, from different providers, side by side in tmux.</dd>
        <dt>NOT FOR</dt>
        <dd>a single agent, an IDE-only setup, or anything outside a terminal multiplexer.</dd>
      </dl>

      <a class="btn btn--primary hero__cta" href="#install">Install</a>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__stack">
      <div class="win hero__win hero__win--driver">
        <div class="win__bar">
          <span class="win__title">pane %1 — Claude Code</span>
          <span class="win__btns"><span class="win__btn"></span><span class="win__btn"></span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="win__body driver__body">
          <span class="ln dv-ln dv-ln--0 entry"><span class="dot"></span><span>Migration written. Before shipping, checking with my pair that it follows the spec&hellip;</span></span>
          <span class="ln dv-ln dv-ln--1 dv-call"><span class="dot dot--call"></span>Calling crossagent <span class="dv-timer dv-timer--a"></span></span>
          <span class="ln dv-ln dv-spin"><span class="spin-star">&#10033;</span> <span class="spin-word"></span></span>
          <span class="ln dv-ln dv-ln--9 entry"><span class="dot"></span><span>Peer wants a rollback path. Adding it.</span></span>
          <span class="ln dv-ln dv-ln--10 entry"><span class="dot dot--reply"></span><span>Update(migrations/0007_add_index.ts)</span></span>
          <span class="ln dv-ln dv-spin dv-spin--2"><span class="spin-star">&#10033;</span> <span class="spin-word spin-word--2"></span></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win hero__win hero__win--reviewer">
        <div class="win__bar">
          <span class="win__title">pane %2 — Codex</span>
          <span class="win__btns"><span class="win__btn"></span><span class="win__btn"></span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="win__body reviewer__body">
          <div class="rv-input rv-ln rv-ln--4 entry"><span class="chev">&rsaquo;</span><span>Hi Astra, Fable here. I just wrote the 0007_add_index migration. Check that it meets the spec.</span></div>
          <span class="ln rv-ln rv-ln--5"><span class="dot dot--rv5"></span>Ran git diff --stat</span>
          <span class="ln rv-ln rv-ln--6"><span class="dot dot--rv6"></span>Ran read 0007_add_index.ts</span>
          <span class="ln rv-ln rv-ln--7 entry"><span class="dot"></span><span><span class="ln--verdict">VERDICT: ADJUST</span> The migration has no rollback. Add a down() step before shipping.</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>


<section class="band band--steps" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="inner">
    <h2 class="h2">How it works.</h2>
    <div class="steps__lead">
      <p>A coding agent reviewing its own work has the same blind spots twice. If you already run two harnesses side by side in tmux, a second opinion is sitting one pane over. You just had to paste between them by hand.</p>
      <p><strong>crossagent</strong> turns that pane into a reviewer. The driver asks over MCP, the peer reads the repo and answers with a verdict, and nothing ships without the other one having a say.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step__n">ping</span>
        <p class="step__txt">Both panes load the same server. Each one declares its pane, harness and repo.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step__n">brief</span>
        <p class="step__txt">The driver briefs the peer once: same-level copilot, reads the repo, never writes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="step__n">discuss</span>
        <p class="step__txt">Every plan and diff goes through discuss. The reply ends in one verdict.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--verdicts" id="verdicts">
  <div class="inner">
    <h2 class="h2">It never just says yes.</h2>
    <div class="verdicts__lead">
      <p>Every reply from the peer ends in one line: the word <code>VERDICT</code> and one of four calls. The driver reads that line before it does anything else.</p>
      <p>The peer is a same-level copilot, not an approver. It reads the repo, runs read-only checks and disagrees when it disagrees. Looping to consensus and escalating stay with the caller. <strong>crossagent</strong> never decides for you.</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="verdicts">
      <div class="verdict verdict--agree">
        <dt class="verdict__word">AGREE</dt>
        <dd class="verdict__def">No corrections. Go ahead and build it.<span class="verdict__next">The driver ships it as is.</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="verdict verdict--adjust">
        <dt class="verdict__word">ADJUST</dt>
        <dd class="verdict__def">Fine once the listed items are fixed.<span class="verdict__next">The driver fixes them, or argues back when one is wrong.</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="verdict verdict--object">
        <dt class="verdict__word">OBJECT</dt>
        <dd class="verdict__def">Do not proceed as written. The reasons come with it.<span class="verdict__next">The driver reworks the plan and asks again.</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="verdict verdict--escalate">
        <dt class="verdict__word">ESCALATE</dt>
        <dd class="verdict__def">Only the human can call this one.<span class="verdict__next">The driver stops and brings it to you.</span></dd>
      </div>
      <div class="verdict verdict--unparsed">
        <dt class="verdict__word">UNPARSED</dt>
        <dd class="verdict__def">Not a verdict. The reply had no readable <code>VERDICT</code> line.<span class="verdict__next">The driver asks again.</span></dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--install" id="install">
  <div class="inner">
    <h2 class="h2">Install.</h2>
    <h3 class="install__title install__title--step">1 &middot; Add the MCP</h3>
    <div class="installs">
      <div class="install">
        <h3 class="install__title">Claude Code</h3>
        <div class="copybox">
          <code class="copybox__cmd">claude mcp add crossagent -- npx -y crossagent-mcp</code>
          <button class="copybox__btn" type="button" data-copy="claude mcp add crossagent -- npx -y crossagent-mcp" aria-label="Copy Claude Code command">
            <svg class="copybox__icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="5" y="5" width="9" height="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/><path d="M11 5V2H2v9h3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/></svg>
            <span class="copybox__label">copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="install">
        <h3 class="install__title">Codex CLI</h3>
        <div class="copybox">
          <code class="copybox__cmd">codex mcp add crossagent -- npx -y crossagent-mcp</code>
          <button class="copybox__btn" type="button" data-copy="codex mcp add crossagent -- npx -y crossagent-mcp" aria-label="Copy Codex CLI command">
            <svg class="copybox__icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="5" y="5" width="9" height="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/><path d="M11 5V2H2v9h3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/></svg>
            <span class="copybox__label">copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="install install--wide">
      <h3 class="install__title">2 &middot; Link the pair skill</h3>
      <div class="copybox">
        <code class="copybox__cmd">npx -y crossagent-mcp setup --link</code>
        <button class="copybox__btn" type="button" data-copy="npx -y crossagent-mcp setup --link" aria-label="Copy link skill command">
          <svg class="copybox__icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="5" y="5" width="9" height="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/><path d="M11 5V2H2v9h3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"/></svg>
          <span class="copybox__label">copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="install__foot install__foot--cta">Using another coding agent? <strong>crossagent</strong> only needs a harness that runs in a tmux pane. Add yours and <a class="install__link" href="https://github.com/k8adev/crossagent" rel="noopener">open a pull request</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<footer class="tmuxbar" aria-label="Site footer">
  <div class="tmuxbar__inner">
    <span class="tmuxbar__session">[crossagent]</span>
    <nav class="tmuxbar__windows" aria-label="Sections">
      <a class="tmuxbar__win" href="#pair" data-win="pair">0:pair<span class="tmuxbar__flag"></span></a>
      <a class="tmuxbar__win" href="#how-it-works" data-win="how-it-works">1:how-it-works<span class="tmuxbar__flag"></span></a>
      <a class="tmuxbar__win" href="#verdicts" data-win="verdicts">2:verdicts<span class="tmuxbar__flag"></span></a>
      <a class="tmuxbar__win" href="#install" data-win="install">3:install<span class="tmuxbar__flag"></span></a>
    </nav>

    <div class="tmuxbar__right">
      <a class="tmuxbar__me" href="https://github.com/k8adev" rel="me">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path fill="currentColor" d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8Z"/>
        </svg>
        <span>k8adev</span>
      </a>
      <a class="tmuxbar__me" href="https://x.com/k8adev" rel="me">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="12" height="12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path fill="currentColor" d="M18.244 2.25h3.308l-7.227 8.26 8.502 11.24H16.17l-5.214-6.817L4.99 21.75H1.68l7.73-8.835L1.254 2.25H8.08l4.713 6.231zm-1.161 17.52h1.833L7.084 4.126H5.117z"/>
        </svg>
        <span>k8adev</span>
      </a>
      <a class="tmuxbar__lic" href="https://github.com/k8adev/crossagent/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
</Base>

<script>
/* tmux window flags: * = section on screen, - = the one before it */
(function(){
  var wins=Array.prototype.slice.call(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.tmuxbar__win[data-win]'));
  var sections=wins.map(function(w){return document.getElementById(w.getAttribute('data-win')||'');}).filter(Boolean) as HTMLElement[];
  if(sections.length<2)return;
  var current='',last='',queued=false;
  var paint=function(){
    wins.forEach(function(w){
      var id=w.getAttribute('data-win');
      w.classList.toggle('tmuxbar__win--current',id===current);
      w.classList.toggle('tmuxbar__win--last',id===last);
    });
  };
  var pick=function(){
    queued=false;
    var probe=window.innerHeight*0.4;
    var best=sections[0].id;
    for(var i=0;i<sections.length;i++){
      if(sections[i].getBoundingClientRect().top<=probe)best=sections[i].id;
    }
    if(window.innerHeight+window.scrollY>=document.documentElement.scrollHeight-2)best=sections[sections.length-1].id;
    if(best!==current){last=current;current=best;paint();}
  };
  var onScroll=function(){if(!queued){queued=true;requestAnimationFrame(pick);}};
  window.addEventListener('scroll',onScroll,{passive:true});
  window.addEventListener('resize',onScroll);
  pick();
})();
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.copybox__btn').forEach(function(btn){
  btn.addEventListener('click',function(){
    var label=btn.querySelector('.copybox__label');
    if(!label)return;
    var done=function(){btn.classList.add('is-copied');label.textContent='copied';setTimeout(function(){btn.classList.remove('is-copied');label.textContent='copy';},1600);};
    if(navigator.clipboard&&navigator.clipboard.writeText){navigator.clipboard.writeText(btn.dataset.copy??'').then(done,function(){label.textContent='select & copy';});}
    else{label.textContent='select & copy';}
  });
});
</script>
